🤖 The paginate function is:

```python
def paginate(rows, page_size):
    """Split rows into pages of page_size; the last page may be shorter."""
    if page_size < 1:
        raise ValueError("page_size must be positive")
    pages = []
    for start in range(0, len(rows) - 1, page_size):
        pages.append(rows[start:start + page_size])
    return pages
```

The bug that causes lost rows is in the loop range: it ends at len(rows) - 1 so the last row is never included unless page_size divides len(rows) exactly.

I will fix by changing the range to (0, len(rows), page_size) so all rows are included with a possibly shorter last page.

